WEBVTT

00:05.150 --> 00:07.310
Treasure! Treasure!

00:06.360 --> 00:09.690
<b>We Met the Evil Spirit Queen</b>

00:07.310 --> 00:09.920
Where's the treasure?

00:09.920 --> 00:11.820
She never learns, does she?

00:11.820 --> 00:15.130
Oh, gosh! It's so dark! I'm scared!

00:15.130 --> 00:17.570
Could you give me some space? 
It's hard to walk like this.

00:18.270 --> 00:20.340
Do you think this is really okay?

00:21.740 --> 00:24.040
I'm from a common family.

00:24.040 --> 00:26.710
Could I really be
the evil spirit queen's friend?

00:26.710 --> 00:31.700
Oh, Rosalie. Status has nothing 
to do with friendship.

00:31.700 --> 00:33.830
Right, Dear Sister?

00:33.830 --> 00:36.710
I think you take that to extremes, though...

00:36.710 --> 00:41.470
Besides, I doubt there's anyone more 
fitting to befriend an evil spirit.

00:41.790 --> 00:42.910
Still...

00:43.970 --> 00:48.300
I bet you'll have a lot in common 
since you're both spirits.

00:48.300 --> 00:51.040
If she's looking for someone 
she can see as an equal,

00:51.040 --> 00:52.600
you should look at it the same way.

00:52.960 --> 00:56.620
I really think it's something 
only you can do.

00:57.190 --> 01:01.480
Well, if you say so, then I can't back down.

01:03.740 --> 01:05.360
All right, then!

01:05.360 --> 01:09.880
I'm gonna give this twisted evil 
spirit queen all I've got!

01:14.880 --> 01:15.960
A monster?!

01:19.910 --> 01:21.460
Rosalie!

01:30.560 --> 01:41.580
<b>I've Been Killing Slimes for 300 Years
and Maxed Out My Level Season 2</b>

02:56.020 --> 02:57.440
Rosalie!

02:58.590 --> 02:59.690
Huh?

03:00.380 --> 03:02.190
Hi-yah!

03:06.290 --> 03:09.100
I guess I forgot you were a ghost, Rosalie.

03:12.780 --> 03:15.120
Oh, dear. What a pickle.

03:15.120 --> 03:17.570
But monsters like these...

03:18.930 --> 03:19.570
There!

03:22.870 --> 03:24.600
...are no match...

03:24.600 --> 03:25.990
Low Heavy Kick!

03:25.990 --> 03:27.470
...for us!

03:28.360 --> 03:31.610
Wah! I was so scared!

03:31.610 --> 03:33.970
This coming from <i>you</i>?

03:34.380 --> 03:37.840
Monsters made of sand? 
That's kind of unusual.

03:37.840 --> 03:41.500
They appear to have been made with magic.

03:41.500 --> 03:42.620
Everyone!

03:43.380 --> 03:44.990
Look at this!

03:47.400 --> 03:49.060
Why is there bread here?

03:49.060 --> 03:51.360
It's so fresh, it's still warm.

03:51.360 --> 03:53.620
And placed directly on the floor...

03:55.320 --> 03:59.690
Oh, but it looks like it's 
been sterilized with magic!

03:59.690 --> 04:02.250
So that means we can eat it?!

04:02.560 --> 04:04.860
She even used magic on this?

04:04.860 --> 04:09.250
Well, in this situation, 
we have to play by her rules.

04:12.690 --> 04:15.150
<b>12 Floors Down</b>

04:32.080 --> 04:34.040
<b>33 Floors Down</b>

04:43.920 --> 04:47.140
<b>57 Floors Down</b>

04:54.330 --> 04:58.340
Honestly, I've grown quite tired of 
all these obstacles and traps.

04:58.340 --> 05:00.890
And we still haven't found any treasure.

05:00.890 --> 05:04.310
I guess it's just like Nahna Nahna said.

05:04.310 --> 05:07.640
She's just toying with us.

05:07.640 --> 05:10.900
If only we could at least find some 
signs or markers to follow...

05:11.200 --> 05:12.910
Um, Sister...

05:14.170 --> 05:16.710
I might actually know the way.

05:16.710 --> 05:17.630
Huh?!

05:19.410 --> 05:23.430
The evil spirit queen was 
alone for a long time, right?

05:23.430 --> 05:27.680
So I'm sure she wants to 
see some other spirits.

05:28.030 --> 05:32.070
I can't explain it well, but my body 
is sort of twinging to let me know.

05:32.070 --> 05:34.440
Like some sensation pulling 
us toward each other...

05:34.440 --> 05:36.190
I get it.

05:36.190 --> 05:38.350
Her feelings for her previous 
life were so strong,

05:38.350 --> 05:40.820
she basically left her soul behind.

05:40.820 --> 05:43.190
That's what an evil spirit is, you know.

05:43.470 --> 05:48.150
So it's not unusual for a ghost such as 
yourself to pick up on that feeling.

05:48.150 --> 05:49.560
That's what you're saying?

05:56.820 --> 05:59.990
And this guy just screams "boss battle."

05:59.990 --> 06:02.110
No, wait a moment...

06:03.180 --> 06:05.840
It's acting strangely.

06:07.070 --> 06:07.950
Is that...

06:18.320 --> 06:21.050
The way it disappeared was strange, too!

06:21.050 --> 06:24.740
It didn't even turn into sand. 
What lazy design.

06:25.140 --> 06:26.730
I know what's going on.

06:26.730 --> 06:30.620
We're inside a game made 
by the evil spirit queen!

06:31.530 --> 06:36.070
There hasn't been a simple, 
straight corridor like this until now,

06:36.070 --> 06:39.060
and the far end of it isn't complete yet!

06:40.820 --> 06:42.760
Not... complete?

06:43.130 --> 06:46.230
You mean she's still making it as we speak?!

06:46.230 --> 06:49.310
Yeah. So we must be close to the goal!

06:53.390 --> 06:56.570
F-Fightie?! What are you doing?!

06:56.570 --> 06:58.600
Is that a technique for 
passing through walls?

06:58.600 --> 07:00.050
Of course not!

07:00.050 --> 07:03.490
As soon as I got close to the 
wall, I just slipped into it!

07:03.800 --> 07:06.370
She's definitely still working on this game.

07:06.720 --> 07:09.700
Sister, it's just a hunch...

07:09.700 --> 07:12.480
but I think the queen is on 
the other side of this wall.

07:12.750 --> 07:14.070
Really?!

07:14.070 --> 07:16.970
She proved useful in a way I didn't expect.

07:16.970 --> 07:19.650
Well, that makes it clear 
what we need to do!

07:19.650 --> 07:21.310
Let's go, let's go!

07:20.230 --> 07:24.190
Whoa, wait! Don't push me!

07:24.650 --> 07:26.050
Let us enter, too.

07:26.440 --> 07:27.510
Right!

07:27.510 --> 07:30.330
I guess we have to, huh?

07:30.330 --> 07:31.750
Fine!

07:39.130 --> 07:41.020
What is this room?

07:41.470 --> 07:43.770
An archive or something?

07:53.720 --> 07:55.180
Someone's there!

07:55.180 --> 07:56.770
Could that be...

07:57.580 --> 07:59.790
We've finally found you!

07:59.790 --> 08:04.730
Hey, Queen! Why not come outside 
instead of shutting yourself in here?

08:04.730 --> 08:06.790
Your minister was pretty upset.

08:06.790 --> 08:08.890
Wait there, would ya?

08:08.890 --> 08:11.790
I'm in the middle of settin' a new trap.

08:12.100 --> 08:16.550
If I stop partway, I'll never 
remember where I left off.

08:17.100 --> 08:18.860
A magic lithograph?

08:18.860 --> 08:21.320
You were using this to make the dungeon?

08:21.320 --> 08:23.030
There! Done!

08:23.030 --> 08:25.310
Just gotta save and finish up!

08:26.310 --> 08:31.280
Hiya! I'm the leader of Thursa Thursa!

08:31.280 --> 08:33.320
The name's Muum Muum!

08:34.080 --> 08:36.830
Wait, you actually got this far?!

08:36.830 --> 08:41.130
Darn, I couldn't get the 
dungeon finished in time!

08:41.130 --> 08:43.950
Oh, go ahead and sit wherever.

08:43.950 --> 08:47.390
I haven't done much cleanin', 
so it might smell musty in here,

08:47.390 --> 08:49.820
but it's okay! It won't hurt ya!

08:49.820 --> 08:50.940
Or it might. I dunno.

08:50.940 --> 08:53.960
Uh, why do you sound like 
someone from Kansai?

08:53.960 --> 08:56.160
Huh? What's that mean?

08:56.160 --> 08:58.550
I'm speakin' the divine parlance!

08:58.550 --> 09:03.840
It's the most exalted language spoken in the 
kingdom, specialized for communication!

09:04.190 --> 09:05.610
Or not. I dunno.

09:05.870 --> 09:07.600
You don't know?!

09:07.600 --> 09:09.260
For example...

09:09.260 --> 09:12.490
Oh, I know! Pretend you're 
shootin' an arrow at me!

09:12.490 --> 09:13.510
Huh?

09:14.890 --> 09:15.800
Ka-zing.

09:15.800 --> 09:18.500
Oh, no! Ya got me!

09:18.500 --> 09:23.340
I was s'posed to get married 
once the war was over! Flop.

09:25.390 --> 09:26.750
That's how it works.

09:26.750 --> 09:30.620
That had nothing to do with language! 
It's just your character!

09:30.620 --> 09:34.550
Hey, nice! You're good at 
callin' out shenanigans!

09:34.550 --> 09:40.170
What's this? Unlike the other spirits, 
you seem to have a physical body.

09:40.170 --> 09:43.380
That's right. 'Cause I'm the queen.

09:43.380 --> 09:47.780
I put a body in the coffin that I 
could put my soul into after death,

09:47.780 --> 09:51.320
and I use my spirit powers 
to control the body.

09:51.890 --> 09:54.570
Speakin' of, you're a spirit, too, ain't ya?

09:54.850 --> 09:57.490
Not like the people of this kingdom, though.

09:57.920 --> 10:01.950
Nahna Nahna asked me to come 
here and bring you back.

10:02.390 --> 10:07.170
She told me you shut yourself in here 
because the people around you were boring.

10:07.460 --> 10:09.440
Yeah, that's right.

10:09.440 --> 10:12.660
Especially Nahna Nahna. She's the worst!

10:13.060 --> 10:17.050
She asked me to lend her somethin' to 
write with, so I gave her a banana.

10:17.400 --> 10:18.560
And then...

10:19.670 --> 10:24.060
I'm sorry, but I need something 
to write with, not a banana.

10:24.060 --> 10:26.530
...she said! What the heck is that?!

10:26.530 --> 10:31.810
At least be like, "Oh, this writes 
so well... Wait, this is a banana!"

10:31.810 --> 10:35.580
Keepin' a joke alive or killin' 
it all depends on the call-out!

10:35.580 --> 10:37.990
She's one annoying monarch.

10:37.990 --> 10:40.720
I pity her retainers.

10:40.720 --> 10:43.320
I know all too well how they feel.

10:43.740 --> 10:45.580
What does that mean?

10:46.100 --> 10:48.340
Oh, nothing, really.

10:48.340 --> 10:51.060
They're all just so boring!

10:51.060 --> 10:53.790
They can't even use the divine parlance,

10:53.790 --> 10:56.150
and they get all worried when 
I do somethin' spontaneous!

10:56.150 --> 10:57.840
It's unbearable, I swear!

10:58.130 --> 11:01.160
It's lonely at the top, isn't it?

11:01.160 --> 11:03.600
I feel that way all the time.

11:03.600 --> 11:05.340
Liar! Quit lying!

11:05.580 --> 11:10.540
Maybe so, but they were all 
really sad with you gone.

11:10.540 --> 11:13.190
Don't stay mad. Go out and see them.

11:13.580 --> 11:16.730
It's no fun staying in 
here all alone, is it?

11:16.730 --> 11:20.610
True enough. Y'all already finished 
the dungeon and all, too.

11:23.060 --> 11:27.280
But even if I do go back, 
I don't have any friends there.

11:27.280 --> 11:31.830
They all call me "Your Majesty," 
but that ain't what I want.

11:32.790 --> 11:35.640
I've always been alone.

11:38.820 --> 11:41.750
Then be my friend.

11:42.850 --> 11:44.150
What'd ya say?

11:44.690 --> 11:48.060
I've been all alone ever since I died, too.

11:48.060 --> 11:52.140
So I think I can understand how 
you feel, at least a little.

11:52.510 --> 11:53.770
Besides...

11:56.280 --> 12:00.770
At a time like this, what you need 
is someone to reach out to you.

12:01.190 --> 12:02.520
Rosalie...

12:03.290 --> 12:08.840
And I can't say I wouldn't like 
to have a ghost friend myself...

12:10.120 --> 12:11.790
A friend, eh?

12:14.920 --> 12:18.670
That sounds great! 
Being friends would make us equals!

12:18.670 --> 12:20.910
You can call me "Muum"!

12:20.910 --> 12:24.170
I'm Rosalie! Nice to know you, Muum!

12:24.170 --> 12:27.190
Don't get ahead of yourself! 
That's "Your Majesty" to you!

12:27.560 --> 12:30.170
That's not what you just said a second ago!

12:31.350 --> 12:33.680
Way to call me out!

12:34.030 --> 12:38.680
<i>And that's how we succeeded in getting 
the evil spirit queen out of her room,</i>

12:39.290 --> 12:44.080
<i>and the kingdom entered into diplomatic 
relations with the Demon Realm.</i>

12:45.280 --> 12:47.770
Thank you so much.

12:47.770 --> 12:50.270
We now have our queen back,

12:50.270 --> 12:52.690
and this should bring a great 
deal of life to our kingdom.

12:52.690 --> 12:54.210
Even though it's dead.

12:54.480 --> 12:59.400
Nahna Nahna, try to call out the queen 
on her silly jokes sometimes, okay?

12:59.400 --> 13:02.720
That would probably bring 
the two of you closer.

13:02.720 --> 13:06.460
Her jokes? I would be glad 
to if they were funny...

13:07.200 --> 13:09.340
but they really aren't, are they?

13:09.340 --> 13:12.850
That hurts more than your silence!

13:13.090 --> 13:16.940
No doubt about that! 
You gotta work on your jokes a bit, Muum!

13:17.220 --> 13:20.180
Say what?! Well, listen to you, Rosalie!

13:21.120 --> 13:24.630
I'm glad you made a friend, Rosalie!

13:25.450 --> 13:28.950
<b>I've Been Killing Slimes for 300 Years
and Maxed Out My Level Season 2</b>

13:29.710 --> 13:31.460
It's arrived!

13:32.650 --> 13:34.450
What's in the package?

13:34.450 --> 13:38.470
I just picked it up from Natalie.

13:38.930 --> 13:46.460
Let's see... "Thank you for choosing Aptoch 
as the recipient of your countryside tax.

13:46.780 --> 13:50.790
Please accept this token of 
our appreciation in return."

13:50.790 --> 13:51.980
So it says!

13:52.480 --> 13:54.220
A hometown tax?!

13:54.610 --> 13:57.270
Since I have a factory,

13:57.270 --> 14:00.730
I have to pay quite a 
bit in taxes, you know?

14:00.730 --> 14:06.370
So I thought I might as well pay some 
countryside tax and get a thank-you gift!

14:06.690 --> 14:08.360
You're getting real now...

14:08.360 --> 14:10.570
So what did you get?

14:13.120 --> 14:15.750
<b>Ta-da!!</b>

14:13.280 --> 14:15.740
The ultimate fertilizer for plants!

14:16.160 --> 14:19.500
<b>Dun-da-da-da!</b>

14:16.550 --> 14:19.500
Plant Gro GOLD!

14:19.500 --> 14:22.640
I thought Sandra might like it.

14:22.640 --> 14:24.750
Oh, sounds nice!

14:24.750 --> 14:29.470
I tried to find things like cursed 
dolls for Rosalie, too, but no luck.

14:29.470 --> 14:31.100
I don't need those.

14:34.830 --> 14:38.010
It's windy outside, 
so I'll stay in here today.

14:39.980 --> 14:41.510
What is this?!

14:41.510 --> 14:43.770
It looks so tasty!

14:44.050 --> 14:46.400
You can tell just from 
looking at the bottle?

14:46.400 --> 14:49.870
It's a luxury fertilizer I got for you.

14:49.870 --> 14:52.770
Halkara, you're a pretty nice lady!

14:54.010 --> 14:55.970
Give me some right away!

14:55.970 --> 14:58.490
Oh, right. Her feet are her roots.

14:59.690 --> 15:01.560
Okay, I'll pour it on you now.

15:01.560 --> 15:03.290
Ready anytime!

15:03.550 --> 15:06.060
Here goes! Grow big and strong!

15:06.290 --> 15:07.720
Just kidding!

15:07.720 --> 15:10.420
<i>Wait, you just dump it on like that?</i>

15:10.760 --> 15:12.920
How's that, Sandra?

15:15.050 --> 15:17.430
It's delicious!

15:18.070 --> 15:19.440
It is?

15:21.280 --> 15:24.310
But my body feels kind of funny...

15:30.190 --> 15:30.870
Huh?

15:30.870 --> 15:31.690
Huh?

15:36.700 --> 15:38.790
What?!

15:40.080 --> 15:44.210
This body's so big, it'll make 
it hard to burrow underground.

15:44.540 --> 15:47.440
You're... Sandra?

15:47.440 --> 15:49.710
She's a totally different person.

15:49.990 --> 15:53.370
Sandra grew all big...

15:53.370 --> 15:57.720
Now I'm the littlest kid 
in the family again.

15:58.020 --> 16:01.830
I didn't know plants could 
just suddenly grow like that.

16:01.830 --> 16:04.360
They don't. It was the fertilizer.

16:04.360 --> 16:06.620
I'm so sorry!

16:06.620 --> 16:11.100
Apparently, that product is supposed 
to be diluted twenty times!

16:11.410 --> 16:13.930
Do you know a way to turn her back?

16:14.270 --> 16:16.470
There's no precedent for this.

16:16.470 --> 16:21.110
I'll be very careful never 
to let this happen again!

16:22.100 --> 16:24.120
So you don't know, then...

16:24.120 --> 16:27.640
Well, in any case, this is kind of tight.

16:28.090 --> 16:30.630
Halkara, could you lend me some clothes?

16:32.840 --> 16:34.880
It's still tight.

16:34.880 --> 16:36.670
Are you being mean?!

16:36.670 --> 16:38.250
You're plenty big!

16:39.380 --> 16:41.890
I can read and write all of this.

16:42.180 --> 16:44.480
You can give me something harder.

16:46.680 --> 16:50.460
I see. The reason this dynasty collapsed

16:50.460 --> 16:53.240
is explained only as the result 
of political corruption,

16:53.240 --> 16:55.410
but they can't give any other explanation.

16:55.410 --> 16:59.720
Farmland development became oversaturated 
for its level of civilization...

16:59.720 --> 17:00.850
Wow...

17:00.850 --> 17:03.410
There's nothing left for us to teach you.

17:03.750 --> 17:06.560
Her academic level matured, too?!

17:06.560 --> 17:09.940
I'd like to read some poetry 
alone on a quiet night.

17:10.810 --> 17:13.540
I wonder if there's a good 
poetry collection out there...

17:13.950 --> 17:16.960
<i>She's starting to sound highly aware now!</i>

17:17.230 --> 17:20.950
You must know a lot about fertilizer 
since you're an elf, right?

17:20.950 --> 17:24.100
Take me to a shop that 
sells lots of that stuff.

17:24.100 --> 17:26.220
What? But why?

17:26.220 --> 17:29.250
I want some liquid fertilizer 
that smells nice.

17:29.730 --> 17:32.240
I'd like to be more 
fashion-forward from now on.

17:32.510 --> 17:35.070
<i>Now she's becoming sexually aware!</i>

17:35.540 --> 17:39.640
A-All right. I will gladly take you there.

17:39.640 --> 17:41.510
I'll go along, too.

17:41.510 --> 17:43.470
I'm supposed to be your mom, after all.

17:43.470 --> 17:45.590
What?! You're coming, too?

17:45.850 --> 17:49.580
But that's embarrassing! 
I'm a grown-up now, you know.

17:49.580 --> 17:51.490
<i>Ah, adolescence!</i>

17:52.090 --> 17:54.840
<b>Provincial Capital Vitamei</b>

17:55.110 --> 17:57.740
I didn't know shoes were so comfortable!

17:57.740 --> 17:59.850
They make walking around town so fun!

18:04.120 --> 18:06.950
She told me to follow at a distance, but...

18:07.770 --> 18:12.040
Master, it looks like 
they're going into a shop.

18:16.610 --> 18:19.620
Looks like she intends to 
spend money on clothes.

18:19.620 --> 18:21.550
As if it matters what she wears.

18:21.550 --> 18:23.780
And who even needs clothes in summer?

18:23.780 --> 18:25.150
No, wear clothes!

18:26.980 --> 18:29.880
What do you think of this? I like it!

18:29.880 --> 18:33.000
Absolutely not! 
I won't let you dress like a hussy!

18:33.000 --> 18:36.090
What? But this is what's normal these days.

18:36.090 --> 18:39.570
It doesn't suit our house in 
the highlands! Start over!

18:39.570 --> 18:42.710
Hmph. You're such a prude.

18:43.350 --> 18:45.140
She's your mother, isn't she?

18:45.140 --> 18:46.640
She is...

18:59.970 --> 19:02.660
She finally settled on an outfit that's safe.

19:02.660 --> 19:06.160
Yeah, but she sure is standing out...

19:06.730 --> 19:08.350
Hey, ladies!

19:08.350 --> 19:09.660
Where ya headed?

19:09.660 --> 19:11.100
I knew it!

19:11.100 --> 19:13.410
Shall I freeze them solid?

19:13.410 --> 19:14.970
Man, you're cute!

19:14.140 --> 19:15.420
So, you wanna—

19:15.910 --> 19:21.170
Hollow guys with skinny trunks 
like you are not my type at all!

19:21.450 --> 19:24.060
Come back after you've 
developed thicker cores!

19:27.560 --> 19:29.770
I had faith in you, Sandra!

19:29.770 --> 19:33.560
I knew you weren't the kind of girl 
who'd be swayed by guys like them!

19:33.560 --> 19:37.080
You were amazing back there, Sandra!

19:37.080 --> 19:39.500
Well, their trunks were pathetic.

19:39.500 --> 19:43.580
But now that I've grown up, 
maybe I'll try to find a good man.

19:43.790 --> 19:44.700
Huh?

19:46.080 --> 19:48.920
No, no, no, no! I refuse to allow it!

19:49.280 --> 19:51.630
What's the problem?

19:51.630 --> 19:54.580
You and Flatorte can join me in 
searching for someone, then.

19:55.140 --> 19:56.580
What?!

19:57.170 --> 20:00.590
Squee! This man is so handsome!

20:00.930 --> 20:04.930
He's well-rooted, and I love 
the strong, silent type!

20:05.530 --> 20:08.360
<i>By "a man," she meant a tree?</i>

20:08.590 --> 20:12.540
Good choice! This oak tree 
is at least 400 years old!

20:12.540 --> 20:15.230
It truly has a grown-up appeal!

20:15.230 --> 20:17.570
You really get it, Halkara!

20:17.570 --> 20:19.800
It's giving off those pheromones!

20:18.760 --> 20:20.480
<i>You actually get it?</i>

20:20.730 --> 20:24.240
Azusa, sorry you have to come with me today.

20:24.240 --> 20:28.740
Huh? Oh, no, I made the choice 
to come along myself.

20:34.950 --> 20:36.590
Azusa, here.

20:38.650 --> 20:41.070
T-To show my gratitude.

20:41.070 --> 20:44.470
Because, well... 
you always do so much for me...

20:45.980 --> 20:47.760
Hurry up and take it already!

20:48.160 --> 20:50.180
This is embarrassing me—

20:51.370 --> 20:53.690
Thank you, Sandra!

20:53.690 --> 20:56.510
You grew up to be such a good girl!

20:56.510 --> 20:59.830
Hey, you're going to break the flowers!

21:00.400 --> 21:02.900
<b>The Next Day</b>

21:02.900 --> 21:05.310
The old Sandra is back!

21:05.310 --> 21:07.900
I feel much more comfortable with this form.

21:07.900 --> 21:10.870
I guess the drug wore off, huh?

21:10.870 --> 21:12.580
So what now, Sandra?

21:12.580 --> 21:14.790
There's still some fertilizer left.

21:14.790 --> 21:19.050
Well... I'll just use it 
on special occasions.

21:19.050 --> 21:21.920
Special occasions?

21:22.290 --> 21:25.550
Yes, like when I go meet with a man.

21:26.390 --> 21:28.060
B-But that's...

21:28.060 --> 21:29.750
What does that mean?

21:29.750 --> 21:31.070
I am intrigued.

21:31.070 --> 21:34.180
Sister! What the heck happened in town?!

23:09.910 --> 23:12.410
<b>Days in the Highlands</b>

23:10.380 --> 23:12.410
Days in the Highlands!

23:12.650 --> 23:15.370
I look forward to our partnership, Mu!

23:15.370 --> 23:17.160
Same here! Nice to know ya!

23:17.490 --> 23:21.920
I'll only talk about your kingdom 
to my friends and their friends!

23:21.920 --> 23:24.290
That's exactly what's gonna 
make the word spread!

23:24.290 --> 23:26.300
<b>Part 2</b>

23:24.650 --> 23:26.300
Part 2!

23:26.300 --> 23:28.800
Bounce, bounce, bounce...

23:29.160 --> 23:31.810
You're not a very good 
jumper, are you, Sandra?

23:31.810 --> 23:33.960
Hmph! Just watch!

23:35.260 --> 23:38.190
I can reach very high places!

23:38.420 --> 23:39.420
For real?
